  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Upgrading TVET Colleges based on the PPDP mode</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNIDO is developing an integrated vocational training system to address the key constraints of TVET system in Ethiopia, with particular focus on automotive assembly, construction machinery assembly, wind generator assembly and installation. This pilot project will improve the policy dialogue, the TVET workshop infrastructure and training curriculum of the TVET system. The project will support the creation pilot automotive, construction machinery and wind generator assembly training center in TVET Colleges jointly selected by the government of Ethiopia and cooperating private sector. UNIDO mobilized private partner companies such as Futon Automotive, Lifan Group and SANY group for the design and implementation of the project.  The government of Ethiopia requested UNIDO to develop a project to unlock key constraints that hinder the development of the TVET sector in the country. A cooperation agreement was signed between UNIDO, the Hunan province of China and the Federal TVET agency of Ethiopia to improve TVET system in selected region of Ethiopia. Subsequently, the UNIDO developed concept note was highly appreciated by Hunan province of China. At the same time UNIDO approached the Permanent Mission China, Ministry of Commerce (MOFCOM), and other partner institutes for possible financing and partnership in this pr</narrative>
  </description>
